  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "pjdysd5fRXEXEJdPKbWjcNtrl/A=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:18:56.520Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Each reactor has its own operation index and assigns monotonically increasing ordinals as operations commit, so **the same logical operation has different ordinals on different reactors.** `pollSyncEnvelopes` therefore mixes two frames of reference in one exchange:\n\n| Field | Direction | Whose ordinals | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `outboxAck` (request) | client \u2192 switchboard | **switchboard's** | client acknowledges switchboard outbox operations it applied |\n| `outboxLatest` (request) | client \u2192 switchboard | **switchboard's** | highest switchboard ordinal the client has seen |\n| `ackOrdinal` (response) | switchboard \u2192 client | **client's** | switchboard acknowledges client-pushed operations it applied |\n| envelope ordinals (response) | switchboard \u2192 client | **switchboard's** | ordinals on outbox operations for the client to track |\n\nThe asymmetry is forced, not accidental. `ackOrdinal` must be in the client's ordinals because the client uses it to trim its own outbox (`trimMailboxFromAckOrdinal`), and those outbox items carry ordinals from the client's index. `outboxAck` must be in the switchboard's ordinals because the switchboard uses it to trim *its* outbox.\n\nThe requirement that falls out: **the client's ordinals must be preserved through the push path** (`pushSyncEnvelopes`), so the switchboard's inbox mailbox can track them and return a meaningful `ackOrdinal`. An implementation that renumbered arriving operations to local ordinals on ingest would break the acknowledgement in a way that looks like a stuck outbox.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor/src/sync/design.md` \u2014 Ordinal Semantics\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:18:56.520Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:18:56.520Z"
    }
  },
